{"id": "unknown-2026-10-30-009", "date": "2026-10-30", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["sustainable_textile", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh’s ESG platform: Can 327 factories win global buyers trust?", "content": "BGMEA has launched an ESG platform to publish factory-reported data from Bangladesh member factories and reduce duplicate information requests.\nAt launch, 326 factories had submitted data; the 2025–26 survey cohort covers 327 factories, about 13.1 per cent of 2,500 active members.\nThe platform does not replace buyer due diligence or audits, and mandatory reporting has no announced date.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-s-esg-platform-can-327-factories-win-global-buyers-trust--314684-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-30-010", "date": "2026-10-30", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "South India's cotton yarn prices steady amid weak demand, cash crunch", "content": "Indian cotton yarn prices stayed stable in Tiruppur and Mumbai as demand remained subdued and payment constraints worsened across the textile value chain.\nTiruppur steadied after a ₹3–5 (~$0.03–0.05) per kg fall earlier this week, while Mumbai faced tight liquidity and limited supply.\nGujarat cotton fell by ₹500 per candy as spinning mills awaited clarity on duty-free import extension.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/south-india-s-cotton-yarn-prices-steady-amid-weak-demand-cash-crunch-314682-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-30-011", "date": "2026-10-30", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.33, "keywords": ["growth", "plunge", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "China drives US Upland cotton sales growth as Pima sales plunge: USDA", "content": "US Upland cotton export sales rose 8 per cent to 216,500 RB in the week ended October 22, with China the top buyer at 52,100 RB and demand also from Turkiye, Vietnam and Indonesia.\nExports fell 18 per cent to 160,800 RB, led by shipments to Vietnam.\nPima cotton demand weakened sharply, with sales down 95 per cent and exports down 56 per cent.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/china-drives-us-upland-cotton-sales-growth-as-pima-sales-plunge-usda-314674-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-30-012", "date": "2026-10-30", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["delay"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Bangladesh customs crackdown tests $1.31 bn fabric imports", "content": "Chattogram Customs locked 467 import consignments in July–September 2026, up 29.4 per cent, with fines and revenue at 582 million taka.\nTexPro puts selected fabric imports at $1.313 billion in July–August, down 2.75 per cent, as China’s share rose to 82.8 per cent.\nApparel exports grew 6.10 per cent, but rule shifts, bond checks and clearance delays are raising compliance and sourcing risks.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-customs-crackdown-tests-1-31-bn-fabric-imports-314678-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-30-013", "date": "2026-10-30", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India's $1 bn fabric exports face new customs rules on Nov 1", "content": "India will require exporters of specified cotton, synthetic and knitted fabrics to declare flame-retardant status in shipping bills from November 1.\nTexPro values the corresponding fabric basket at $1.037 billion in FY 2025-26, with April-July 2026 exports up 3.79 per cent to $337.03 million.\nPLI Round 4 opens the same day; Sri Lanka and Bangladesh made up about 42.3 per cent of exports.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-1-bn-fabric-exports-face-new-customs-rules-on-nov-1-314677-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-30-014", "date": "2026-10-30", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth", "increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "US' Crocs raises FY26 outlook as HeyDude returns to growth", "content": "Crocs has lifted its FY26 revenue growth outlook to about 3 per cent and adjusted diluted earnings per share guidance to $14.45-$14.65 after robust Q3 execution. \nThird-quarter revenue rose 4.6 per cent to $1.04 billion and net income increased 48.7 per cent to $216.8 million.  \nHeyDude revenue climbed 6.1 per cent, returning to growth, while Crocs Brand international sales rose 11.8 per cent. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/us-crocs-raises-fy26-outlook-as-heydude-returns-to-growth-314675-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-30-015", "date": "2026-10-30", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["fast_fashion", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "US' Columbia raises FY26 sales outlook after stronger Q3", "content": "Columbia Sportswear has raised the low end of its FY26 sales and diluted earnings per share outlook after a stronger-than-expected third quarter, supported by earlier wholesale shipments, improving US DTC trends and international momentum. \nQ3 net sales rose 2 per cent to $962.6 million and net income increased to $84.7 million from $52 million. \nOperating margin reached 11.4 per cent. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/us-columbia-raises-fy26-sales-outlook-after-stronger-q3-314658-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-30-016", "date": "2026-10-30", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "EU takes 49% of Bangladesh RMG exports: What happens after EBA?", "content": "Bangladesh’s EU EBA garment preferences could continue to end-2029 after its scheduled LDC graduation on November 24, 2026, or to end-2032 if the UN approves an extension.\nRegulation (EU) 2026/1395 grants a three-year transition, but rules of origin will shape future apparel eligibility.\nThe EU took $19.06 billion, or 49.25 per cent, of Bangladesh’s FY2025–26 RMG exports.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/eu-takes-49-of-bangladesh-rmg-exports-what-happens-after-eba--314655-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
